1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,924
Feature A works.

2
00:00:01,924 --> 00:00:05,219
Feature B works. Feature C works.

3
00:00:05,219 --> 00:00:08,019
But what happens when they work together?

4
00:00:08,019 --> 00:00:12,163
Safe alone. Dangerous together. Meet DoNotMix.

5
00:00:12,163 --> 00:00:19,621
In our demo store, every feature flag passes every scenario on its own. Seventy out of seventy tests are green.

6
00:00:19,621 --> 00:00:34,654
Flagsmith is the source of truth. DoNotMix reads the live Staging environment through the official Flagsmith CLI: flags, segments, and the full environment document, including a segment override that turns AI search on for beta testers.

7
00:00:34,654 --> 00:00:51,464
Ten flags means one thousand and twenty-four states. DoNotMix builds a covering array that hits every three-way combination in twenty-five states, and runs the real test suite on each, evaluated by the Flagsmith SDK, segment overrides included. Sixteen seconds.

8
00:00:51,464 --> 00:00:55,478
The verdict: the current Staging state is already broken.

9
00:00:55,478 --> 00:01:11,197
Three flags together make checkout charge the wrong amount, with no error at all. Delta debugging shrinks the failure to exactly those three flags. Flipping any one of them makes the test pass, and no combination of the other seven flags makes the failure go away.

10
00:01:11,197 --> 00:01:17,959
It also finds a crash that needs two flags, and a payment bug that only appears when a flag is switched off.

11
00:01:17,959 --> 00:01:23,895
And one that only beta users hit, because a Flagsmith segment override changes their mix.

12
00:01:23,895 --> 00:01:44,516
Measured, not claimed. At the same small test budget, DoNotMix finds about ninety percent of planted faults, where random testing finds about seventy. Minimization recovers the exact cause in over ninety percent of cases, with zero false positives. Where it lost, at the tiniest budget on our demo app, we say so.

13
00:01:44,516 --> 00:01:53,686
Fixing Staging is a human decision. DoNotMix proposes the smallest flag change, and verifies it against the tests before anyone sees it.

14
00:01:53,686 --> 00:01:57,789
An agent cannot approve it, and cannot apply it without approval.

15
00:01:57,789 --> 00:02:10,321
A human approves by typing the environment name. Apply then checks that nothing drifted, changes exactly the approved flags through the Flagsmith CLI, re-scans, and writes a tamper-evident audit log.

16
00:02:10,321 --> 00:02:23,673
Your coding agent can run the whole workflow with the DoNotMix Agent Skill. In a measured A B test it used sixteen percent fewer tokens and half the tool calls, completed every run, and never changed a flag without approval.

17
00:02:23,673 --> 00:02:30,486
One docker compose up gives you self-hosted Flagsmith, the demo store, a first scan and the dashboard.

18
00:02:30,486 --> 00:02:36,024
DoNotMix. Find the combinations that break your app, before your users do.
